{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "25", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "12", "M": "22", "S": "59"}}, "news": [{"title": "The House of Abhinandan Lodha & NITCO to jointly develop mixed-use project in Alibaug", "para": "The House of Abhinandan Lodha, through its subsidiary HoABL Impactum Land, has signed an MoU with NITCO, NITCO Realties and promoter Vivek Talwar to develop land parcels in Alibaug. The project is expected to generate \u20b93,000 crore revenue for HoABL and \u20b91,500 crore for NITCO over five years.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/the-house-of-abhinandan-lodha-nitco-to-jointly-develop-mixed-use-project-in-alibaug/133506400?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-379224/133506400.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Schindler India launches new experience centre in Gurugram; reinforcing our commitment to sustainable urban mobility", "para": "Schindler India has unveiled its new Experience Centre in Gurugram, highlighting advancements in vertical mobility solutions. During the launch, a panel of experts deliberated on creating sustainable, interconnected urban spaces in the Delhi-NCR region by 2030. They stressed the importance of transit-oriented development, walkable neighborhoods, and eco-friendly construction practices, while also calling for supportive policies. Schindler reaffirmed its commitment to Net Zero and introduced an environmentally conscious maintenance contract.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/brand-connect-initiative/schindler-india-launches-new-experience-centre-in-gurugram-reinforcing-our-commitment-to-sustainable-urban-mobility/133500835?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-78140/133500835.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "brand-connect-initiative"}, {"title": "Property tax powers Chandigarh civic body's \u20b9134 crore own revenue haul", "para": "During the months of April to June, property tax became a cornerstone of the Chandigarh municipal corporation's finances, yielding over Rs 134 crore in revenue. This surge was partly due to timely rebates provided to taxpayers. The civic authority, however, faced expenses of Rs 254 crore, primarily from salaries. A notable amount was dedicated to crucial development initiatives, particularly in road construction and upgrades.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/property-tax-powers-chandigarh-civic-bodys-134-crore-own-revenue-haul/133493794?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-112024/133493794.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}